ki-dark-bg:#0B0C0E;color:#1f2328;--shiki-dark:#D4D4D4" language="shellscript"><code language="shellscript" numberOfLines="17"><span class="line"><span style="color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#DCDCAA">curl</span><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178"> https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions</span><span style="color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#D7BA7D"> \</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#569CD6">  -H</span><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178"> &quot;Authorization: Bearer &lt;OPENROUTER_API_KEY&gt;&quot;</span><span style="color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#D7BA7D"> \</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#569CD6">  -H</span><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178"> &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot;</span><span style="color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#D7BA7D"> \</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#569CD6">  -d</span><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178"> &#x27;{</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">    &quot;models&quot;: [</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">      &quot;anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5&quot;,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">      &quot;openai/gpt-5-mini&quot;,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">      &quot;google/gemini-3-flash-preview&quot;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">    ],</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">    &quot;messages&quot;: [{ &quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;Hello&quot; }],</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">    &quot;provider&quot;: {</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">      &quot;sort&quot;: {</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">        &quot;by&quot;: &quot;price&quot;,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">        &quot;partition&quot;: &quot;none&quot;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">      }</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">    }</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#CE9178">  }&#x27;</span></span>
</code></pre></div></div></div></div><div class="code-block-fade-overlay print:hidden" data-fade-overlay="true" aria-hidden="true" style="--fade-color-light:#ffffff;--fade-color-dark:#0B0C0E"></div></div></div></div>
<span data-as="p">In this example, if you have a BYOK key configured for OpenAI but not for Anthropic, OpenRouter can route to the GPT-4o endpoint using your own key even though Claude is listed first. Without <code>partition: &quot;none&quot;</code>, the router would always try Claude’s endpoints first before falling back to GPT-4o.</span>
<div role="note" aria-label="Note" class="callout my-4 px-5 py-4 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl flex gap-3 border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50 dark:border-blue-900 dark:bg-blue-600/20" data-callout-type="note"><div class="mt-0.5 w-4" data-component-part="callout-icon"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18" stroke-width="1.5" class="size-4 text-blue-800 dark:text-blue-300"><use href="#mi-mint-1-CalloutNote"></use></svg></div><div class="text-sm prose dark:prose-invert min-w-0 w-full [&amp;_kbd]:bg-background-light dark:[&amp;_kbd]:bg-background-dark [&amp;_code]:text-current! [&amp;_kbd]:text-current! [&amp;_a]:text-current! [&amp;_a]:border-current [&amp;_strong]:text-current! text-blue-800 dark:text-blue-300" data-component-part="callout-content"><span data-as="p">BYOK endpoints are automatically prioritized when you have API keys configured for a provider and the request sets no <code>order</code>. The <code>partition: &quot;none&quot;</code> setting allows this prioritization to work across model boundaries. A request that sets <code>order</code> is routed in that order, with your BYOK endpoint tried first within each provider you name; see <a class="link" href="/docs/guides/overview/auth/byok#byok-with-provider-ordering">BYOK with Provider Ordering</a>.</span></div></div>
<h2 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="ordering-specific-providers"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#ordering-specific-providers" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18" stroke-width="2" class="size-3 shrink-0"><use href="#mi-mint-1-Link"></use></svg></div></a></div><span class="cursor-pointer">Ordering Specific Providers</span></h2>
<span data-as="p">You can set the providers that OpenRouter will prioritize for your request using the <code>order</code> field.</span>
<!-- --><div role="presentation" style="position:relative;--scroll-area-corner-height:0px;--scroll-area-corner-width:0px" data-component-part="scroll-area" data-table-wrapper="true" class="min-w-0 [--page-padding:20px] flex w-[calc(100%+(var(--page-padding)*2))] my-[1em] py-[1em] -mx-(--page-padding) max-w-none [contain:inline-size]"><div data-id="base-ui-_R_82aqqelubqoqe9qj4npfiutb_-viewport" tabindex="-1" class="size-full rounded-[inherit] [--scroll-area-fade-size:32px] overflow-y-hidden! base-ui-disable-scrollbar" style="overflow:scroll" data-component-part="scroll-area-viewport" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable table"><div role="presentation" style="min-width:fit-content" data-component-part="scroll-area-content" class="flex"><div class="px-(--page-padding) grow max-w-none table"><table class="m-0 min-w-full w-full max-w-none table [&amp;_th]:text-left [&amp;_td[data-numeric]]:tabular-nums [&amp;_td]:min-w-[150px]"><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>order</code></td><td>string[]</td><td data-numeric="true">-</td><td>List of provider slugs to try in order (e.g. <code>[&quot;anthropic&quot;, &quot;openai&quot;]</code>).</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div>
<span data-as="p">The router will prioritize providers in this list, and in this order, for the model you’re using. The order also outranks the priority your <a class="link" href="/docs/guides/overview/auth/byok#byok-with-provider-ordering">BYOK keys</a> would otherwise get: within each provider you name, your own key is tried before OpenRouter’s shared capacity. If you don’t set this field, the router will <a href="#price-based-load-balancing-default-strategy" class="link">load balance</a> across the top providers to maximize uptime.</span>
<div role="note" aria-label="Tip" class="callout my-4 px-5 py-4 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl flex gap-3 border border-green-200 bg-green-50 dark:border-green-900 dark:bg-green-600/20 [&amp;_[data-component-part=&#x27;callout-icon&#x27;]]:mt-px" data-callout-type="tip"><div class="mt-0.5 w-4" data-component-part="callout-icon"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18" stroke-width="1.5" class="size-4.5 text-green-800 dark:text-green-300"><use href="#mi-mint-1-CalloutTip"></use></svg></div><div class="text-sm prose dark:prose-invert min-w-0 w-full [&amp;_kbd]:bg-background-light dark:[&amp;_kbd]:bg-background-dark [&amp;_code]:text-current! [&amp;_kbd]:text-current! [&amp;_a]:text-current! [&amp;_a]:border-current [&amp;_strong]:text-current! text-green-800 dark:text-green-300" data-component-part="callout-content"><span data-as="p">You can use the copy button next to provider names on model pages to get the exact provider slug, including any variants like “/turbo”. See <a href="#targeting-specific-provider-endpoints" class="link">Targeting Specific Provider Endpoints</a> for details.</span></div></div>
<span data-as="p">OpenRouter will try them one at a time and proceed to other providers if none are operational. If you don’t want to allow any other providers, you should <a href="#disabling-fallbacks" class="link">disable fallbacks</a> as well.</span>
<h3 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="example-specifying-providers-with-fallbacks"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#example-specifying-providers-with-fallbacks" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18" stroke-width="2" class="size-3 shrink-0"><use href="#mi-mint-1-Link"></use></svg></div></a></div><span class="cursor-pointer">Example: Specifying providers with fallbacks</span></h3>
<span data-as="p">This example skips over OpenAI (which doesn’t host Mixtral), tries Together, and then falls back to the normal list of providers on OpenRouter:</span>
<div data-orientation="horizontal" data-activation-direction="none" class="code-group p-0.5 mt-5 mb-8 flex flex-col not-prose relative rounded-2xl border border-gray-950/10 dark:border-white/10 min-w-0 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-white/5 dark:codeblock-dark text-gray-950 dark:text-gray-50 codeblock-light"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 relative pr-2.5" data-component-part="code-group-tab-bar"><div role="presentation" style="position:relative;--scroll-area-corner-height:0px;--scroll-area-corner-width:0px" data-component-part="scroll-area" class="min-w-0 flex-1 w-0 rounded-tl-xl"><div data-id="base-ui-_R_l8qaqqelubqoqe9qj4npfiutb_-viewport" tabindex="-1" class="size-full rounded-[inherit] [--scroll-area-fade-size:32px] overflow-y-hidden! base-ui-disable-scrollbar" style="overflow:scroll" data-component-part="scroll-area-viewport"><div role="presentation" style="min-width:fit-content" data-component-part="scroll-area-content"><div data-orientation="horizontal" data-activation-direction="none" role="tablist" aria-label="Code examples" class="text-xs leading-6 gap-1 flex"><button type="button" data-active="" data-orientation="horizontal" data-activation-direction="none" aria-disabled="false" tabindex="-1" role="tab" aria-selected="true" id="base-ui-_R_2ql8qaqqelubqoqe9qj4npfiutb_" data-composite-item-active="" class="group flex items-center relative gap-1.5 my-1 mb-1.5 outline-0 whitespace-nowrap font-medium ml-0! first:ml-2.5! focus-visible:outline-hidden text-primary dark:text-primary-light"><div class="peer/title flex items-center gap-1.5 px-1.5 rounded-lg z-10 group-focus-visible:outline-1 group-focus-visible:outline-primary dark:group-focus-visible:outline-primary-light group-hover:bg-gray-200/50 dark:group-hover:bg-gray-700/70 group-hover:text-primary dark:group-hover:text-primary-light">TypeScript SDK</div><div class="absolute -bottom-1.5 left-0 right-0 h-0.5 rounded-full bg-primary dark:bg-primary-light peer-empty/title:hidden"></div></button><button 