or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`ignore`}),`), it matches `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`all`}),` eligible endpoints for that provider, including any variants or regions. For example, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"google-vertex\"`}),` matches `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`google-vertex`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`google-vertex/us-east5`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`google-vertex/us-central1`}),`, and so on. A base slug does not by itself opt into a `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/guides/features/service-tiers`,children:`service tier endpoint`}),` (e.g. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`openai/fast`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`google-vertex/flex`}),`); select one with the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`service_tier`}),` parameter or its tier-suffixed slug. Tier endpoints already in the routing pool, such as priority endpoints of open-weight models, do match their base slug.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`To target a `,_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`specific`}),` variant or region, use the full slug including the suffix (e.g. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"google-vertex/us-east5\"`}),` or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"deepinfra/turbo\"`}),`). When a provider serves the same variant from more than one region, the region follows the variant as its own segment (e.g. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"baseten/fp4/us\"`}),`); the variant slug alone (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"baseten/fp4\"`}),`) still matches every region of it.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Every endpoint slug has the shape `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`provider[/variant][/region][/tier]`}),`, with each segment present only when the endpoint needs it: the variant (a quantization such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`fp4`}),`, or a provider-specific label such as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`zdr`}),`), then the region, then the `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/guides/features/service-tiers`,children:`service tier`}),` in the provider’s spelling (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`priority`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`fast`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`turbo`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`flex`}),`), always last. A tier endpoint’s slug is therefore its standard sibling’s slug plus the tier (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`google-vertex/global`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`google-vertex/global/priority`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`baseten/fp4/us`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`baseten/fp4/us/priority`}),`), and dropping a trailing segment matches every endpoint that shares the remaining prefix, except that dropping the tier never matches a tier endpoint.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(Table,{children:[_jsx(_components.thead,{children:_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.th,{children:`Slug in request`}),_jsx(_components.th,{children:`What it matches`})]})}),_jsxs(_components.tbody,{children:[_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"google-vertex\"`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`All Google Vertex endpoints (every region)`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"google-vertex/us-east5\"`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Only the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`us-east5`}),` region endpoint`]})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"deepinfra\"`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`All DeepInfra endpoints (default + turbo)`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`\"deepinfra/turbo\"`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:`Only the DeepInfra turbo endpoint`})]})]})]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`example-targeting-a-specific-endpoint-variant`,children:`Example: Targeting a specific endpoint variant`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`For 